Only the camera wearer is present. They face downward toward a raised garden bed less than arm’s length away. A bag of dark organic material is held directly in front of them, and the surrounding mature plants are within easy reach. The brick walkway is immediately beside the bed, with a parked car several metres beyond; nobody is obstructing or crossing the wearer’s path.

The wearer appears ready to distribute the material around the established plants. Spreading it evenly is the most appropriate action because this avoids concentrated nutrients and supports balanced growth.

